when the well is right (13903 residues): |error|  10.93 deg mean, 84.5% within 20
when it is wrong      (4076 residues): |error| 102.15 deg mean

Reading it: predictions sitting as close to the wells as the natives do,
with a well-match rate near chance, is well *selection* failing -- the
rule picks real rotamers and picks wrong. Predictions sitting markedly
further from the wells than the natives is *averaging* -- the rule lands
between wells, at an angle no side chain occupies, which is what a von
Mises NLL against the native rewards when it cannot resolve the mode.

